# Per-feature verify scripts, sourced by tools/verify_all.sh. Each calls ok "..." or bad "...".
# Each script starts with what it watches, for `verify_all.sh --changed` (tools/verify_select.py):
#   # watch: @core examples/my-feature/** tools/verify.d/my_feature_*.py   (repo paths; * within a dir, ** across, !excl)
#   # needs: 4k                                (units whose $V output it reads, so they run with it; optional)
# @core = the cad wrapper, cadcheck, cadq and cadlib; @layer = printcheck (verify_all.sh's #@ group lines). The script
# itself is always watched. It runs when a watched path changes, a code line of it changes, or a unit it needs: is
# selected for a change of its own. A script with no `# watch:` runs on every --changed run ("no watch header").
# verify_select.sh (runs on every --changed run) checks that every $ROOT path, Python os.path.join(ROOT|HERE, ...)
# path, cad subcommand and layer check in it is in its watch, and its $V reads are needed. Under --changed a selected
# script that calls neither ok nor bad fails the run; call nochecks "why" when there is honestly nothing to check.
